      "text": "I implemented `format` in `format.ts` for all the conversions in the README (`d i x X o e E f F g G s c` and `%%`). The export and signature are unchanged. I ran one quick spot check with `tsx` and the output matched what I expected from the README rules. I did not run any broader tests.\n\n- **Rounding:** floats are converted to their exact binary value using `BigInt`, then rounded half-to-even. That gives `%.2f` of 2.675 as `2.67` and `%.0f` of 2.5 as `2`.\n- **What the spot check covered:**\n  - `%g` and `%G` style selection (`0.0001234`, `1e+20`, `1E-10`)\n  - `%e` (`1.234568e+04`)\n  - zero padding after the sign (`-003.142`)\n  - precision on integers (`+007`)\n  - the `#` flag (`010`, `0xff`)\n  - left-justified width (`42   `)\n  - `%s` precision and `%c` width\n- **Not checked:** `-0`, `Infinity` and `NaN`, bigint arguments, the `%#g` and `%#e` paths, and very large or subnormal values.\n\nI created a temporary test file to run the check and deleted it afterwards.",
